The conjecture is true! Here is a proof.

Axiom 2 (implies_2): implies(true, X) = X.
Axiom 3 (opOr_2): opOr(true, X) = true.
Axiom 4 (opOr_1): opOr(false, X) = X.
Axiom 5 (eqNat_1): eqNat(zero, zero) = true.
Axiom 6 (eqNat_2): eqNat(zero, suc(X)) = false.
Axiom 7 (eqNat_3): eqNat(suc(X), zero) = false.
Axiom 8 (headNat_1): headNat(cons_nat(X, Y)) = X.
Axiom 11 (elemNat_2): elemNat(X, cons_nat(Y, Z)) = opOr(eqNat(X, Y), elemNat(X, Z)).
Axiom 12 (prop_elemHead_1): prop_elemHead(X, Y) = implies(elemNat(X, Y), eqNat(headNat(Y), X)).

Goal 1 (prop_elemHead): prop_elemHead(X, Y) = false.
The goal is true when:
  X = zero
  Y = cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X))

Proof:
  prop_elemHead(zero, cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X)))
= { by axiom 12 (prop_elemHead_1) }
  implies(elemNat(zero, cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X))), eqNat(headNat(cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X))), zero))
= { by axiom 11 (elemNat_2) }
  implies(opOr(eqNat(zero, suc(Y)), elemNat(zero, cons_nat(zero, X))), eqNat(headNat(cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X))), zero))
= { by axiom 6 (eqNat_2) }
  implies(opOr(false, elemNat(zero, cons_nat(zero, X))), eqNat(headNat(cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X))), zero))
= { by axiom 4 (opOr_1) }
  implies(elemNat(zero, cons_nat(zero, X)), eqNat(headNat(cons_nat(suc(Y), cons_nat(zero, X))), zero))
= { by axiom 8 (headNat_1) }
  implies(elemNat(zero, cons_nat(zero, X)), eqNat(suc(Y), zero))
= { by axiom 7 (eqNat_3) }
  implies(elemNat(zero, cons_nat(zero, X)), false)
= { by axiom 11 (elemNat_2) }
  implies(opOr(eqNat(zero, zero), elemNat(zero, X)), false)
= { by axiom 5 (eqNat_1) }
  implies(opOr(true, elemNat(zero, X)), false)
= { by axiom 3 (opOr_2) }
  implies(true, false)
= { by axiom 2 (implies_2) }
  false

RESULT: Theorem (the conjecture is true).
